    qwen36 DFlash2: the e8m0 GEMV scale fix (bit-exact, 248 GB/s) + the launch-gap quantification - the graph port is the quality-lossless lever for BOTH fronts
    
    The e8m0 scalar GEMV computed its power-of-two scale with exp2f (a
    transcendental) per 4 elements; __uint_as_float(code << 23) is bit-exact
    and one instruction. Standalone: 228 -> 248 GB/s (pure-read ceiling
    266-276). In-situ the gain is mostly absorbed by launch overhead - the
    FFN arithmetic quantifies it: 76.2ms/frame in-situ vs ~72.5ms of kernel
    math -> ~4ms FFN launch gaps + ~5ms GDN = 8-10ms/frame no-spec (~8%) and
    ~16ms/round spec (~9%). ONE CUDA graph per frame shape recovers both.
    
